+= Feel++ Coding Rules Audit
+:toc:
+
+This audit reconciles the documentation sets (`general`, `cpp20`, `hpc`) with the current repository tooling.
+External documentation links could not be fetched in this offline environment; items flagged with ⚠️ should be
+verified against the upstream docs before merging.
+
+== Summary Matrix
+
+[cols="1,1,1,1,1", options="header"]
+|===
+| Topic | Current Source | Proposed Canonical Rule | Rationale | Impact / Notes
+| Brace style & indentation | `.clang-format` (Allman + 4 spaces) vs docs (⚠️ verify) | Allman braces with 4-space indent and flush-left namespaces using the compact `namespace feelpp::foo {` form | Matches long-standing Feel++ style while avoiding diff noise | `.clang-format`, AGENTS, CONTRIBUTING
+| Column width | Historical `.clang-format` used `ColumnLimit: 0` vs docs (⚠️ verify) | Keep no hard column limit | Prevents unintentional reflow of legacy code | `.clang-format`, AGENTS guidance
+| Pointer alignment | `.clang-format` pins `PointerAlignment: Left` | Keep pointer aligned with the type | Consistent with HPC kernels and existing codebase | `.clang-format`
+| Short statements | Legacy config allowed compact `if`/function bodies | Allow short functions on a single line and permit one-line `if` statements | Preserves existing formatting expectations | `.clang-format`
+| Namespace formatting | Docs emphasise nested namespaces; repo historically used manual concatenation | Enable `modernize-concat-nested-namespaces` and require compact namespaces without indentation | Ensures C++17 nested namespace syntax while keeping layout stable | `.clang-format`, `.clang-tidy`, AGENTS
